      en: "Drammen Museum is an open-air museum founded in 1909, preserving Buskerud's cultural history. It includes several historic buildings such as the Tangen Gård manor from 1790 and an old water mill. The collection holds over 50,000 artifacts illustrating bourgeois and rural life. Special emphasis is placed on the timber trade that fueled Drammen's growth in the 18th and 19th centuries. The museum hosts around 40,000 visitors annually.",
