      en: "Alta Museum (Alta museum) is a cultural history museum in Alta, Finnmark. It is famous for the nearby Alta rock art, a UNESCO World Heritage site dating from 5,000 to 2,000 BCE. The museum exhibits Sami culture, mining and fishing history. Opened in 1984, it attracts about 100,000 visitors annually. The building is built into the hillside, blending with the landscape. The permanent exhibition displays over 6,000 rock carvings in situ. It also covers WWII resistance. The museum conducts archaeological research and has a large collection of artifacts.",
